  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Strong to severe showers and thunderstorms into\nthis evening with additional chances for daily thunderstorms \nthrough mid week.\n\nBest severe parameters are in the Piedmont with SBCAPEs of 3000\nto 4000 J/kg, and DCAPEs exceeding 1000 J/kg.\n\nMain concern will be from wet microbursts as best shear is\nfurther north. Storms in the mountains could get strong, but\nradar trends show many cells competing with each other and this\nwill tend to keep instability limited. However, training of\ncells in the mountains could cause flooding concerns. We've been\ndry the last 3+ days for most of the area, so flooding would be\nvery localized.\n\n\n5h trough axis will be over us tonight, and should drive the\nfront further south Sunday. Seems severe and flooding threat\nwould be limited to our NC counties if that tomorrow.\nShowers/storms will could be scattered/numerous with the front\novernight tonight, the lower clouds may hinder instability\nSunday along/north of the front.\n\nAs the upper trough position amplifies and the fronts work \nsoutheast through early-mid next week, heavy convective rain \nchances will overspread much of the area thanks to a slow wavy \nfrontal progression. \n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...Temperatures will be seasonable for late mid-late July, and\ncooldown after next frontal passage late week.\n\nPattern with 2 fronts and troughiness will lead to temperatures\nrunning at/close to normal early in the period but still on the\nhumid side, then after the frontal passage midweek, should see\ntemperatures slightly below normal.",
